The design and much of the code of src/tpde/ (the analyzer, compiler core,
arm64 and x86-64 layers, assembler and object writers, and the TIR test IR)
are translated from TPDE's C++ sources and modified: files carrying TPDE's
copyright line are such ports. Changes from TPDE's behaviour are listed in
docs/PLAN.md ("Where we differ from TPDE"). The CIR IR, the tools and the
tests are new.

The instruction encoders (src/tpde/a64/enc.coil, src/tpde/x64/enc.coil) are
written for this package; they take the roles of disarm64 and fadec in TPDE,
and the x86-64 NOP sequences follow fadec. Both are by Alexis Engelke under the
BSD 3-Clause license (LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-disarm.txt,
LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-fadec.txt).

